kwin 6.7: keep advertising kde_output_device_v2 globals per output

Have the registry register each device as a wl_global of its own, as
6.6 did. The generated server class supports being both: a bind through the
global and a registry announcement land in the same resource map, so the
initial state, updates and the removed event reach both kinds of binder.
Plasma's own clients bind only the registry object, so they see no duplicates.

The global is retired the way kwin retires wl_output: on withdrawal the
device sends removed, stops following its output and unpublishes the global
with wl_global_remove, deleting itself once the global can be destroyed. A
hard wl_global_destroy on withdrawal is fatal with libwayland 1.26 and
wl_fixes v2 (advertised by 6.7.4): a client acknowledging the removal of an
already destroyed global is disconnected with "the given registry did not
announce global N", which is how plasmashell died whenever a virtual output
went away. A client binding the retired global late is only told it is gone,
and configurations naming it are ignored as for a destroyed device.

Applies to kwin 6.7.x (verified against v6.7.4 and v6.7.5).

--- a/src/wayland/outputdevice_v2.h
+++ b/src/wayland/outputdevice_v2.h
@@ -65,7 +65,25 @@
 
     static OutputDeviceV2Interface *get(wl_resource *native);
 
+    /**
+     * Additionally advertise this device as a kde_output_device_v2 global of
+     * its own, as kwin before 6.7 did, so clients enumerating output devices
+     * through wl_registry rather than kde_output_device_registry_v2 still
+     * find it. Resources bound either way share one resource map.
+     */
+    void announceGlobal(Display *display);
+
+    /**
+     * Withdraw the device: every bound client gets the removed event and the
+     * device stops following its output. A device announced as a global is
+     * then unpublished the way wl_output is, and deletes itself once the
+     * global can go away (every registry acknowledged the removal, or the
+     * deferred destroy fired); a device without one is deleted right away.
+     */
+    void remove();
+
 private:
+    void retire();
     void updatePhysicalSize();
     void updateGlobalPosition();
     void updateManufacturer();
